{
  "id": "e1",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "title": "Todo API: the classic three",
  "minutes": 15,
  "tagline": "Missing await, missing return, query strings that aren't booleans.",
  "tags": ["async/await", "response flow", "query params"],
  "lookFor": [
    "Every repository call is async. Is every one of them awaited?",
    "After res.json(...) in an if-block, is there a return?",
    "Everything in req.query is a string. Comparing it to a boolean or number will quietly match nothing."
  ],
  "bugs": [
    {
      "symptom": "POST /todos returns an empty object",
      "file": "src/routes/todos.js",
      "hints": [
        "The test gets `{}` back. What does JSON.stringify do to a Promise?",
        "Look at the line that calls repo.create(...). What does an async function return if you don't await it?"
      ],
      "cause": "`repo.create()` is async but isn't awaited, so `todo` is a pending Promise. `res.json(promise)` turns it into `{}`. The insert still finishes later, so the data shows up 'eventually'. That makes it a nasty one to spot in production.",
      "fix": "`const todo = await repo.create({ title: title.trim() });`",
      "pattern": "Missing await"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "A todo with no title crashes after the 400 is sent",
      "file": "src/routes/todos.js",
      "hints": [
        "The 400 response IS sent. So why does the test still fail with an error after that?",
        "Does code keep running after `res.status(400).json(...)`?"
      ],
      "cause": "`res.json()` sends the response but does NOT stop the function. Execution falls through to `title.trim()` (crashes on undefined) or, for a whitespace title, creates an empty todo and tries to send a second response (ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT).",
      "fix": "`return res.status(400).json({ error: 'title is required' });`",
      "pattern": "Missing return after sending a response"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "?done=true returns nothing",
      "file": "src/routes/todos.js",
      "hints": [
        "Log `typeof req.query.done` in the GET handler.",
        "Stored value: boolean `true`. Filter value: string `'true'`. Strict equality."
      ],
      "cause": "Query params are always strings. The filter becomes `{ done: 'true' }`, which never strictly equals the stored boolean `true`.",
      "fix": "`filter.done = req.query.done === 'true';`",
      "pattern": "Query params are strings"
    }
  ]
}
@@@ ticket.md
# TODO-142: Todo service is flaky

A small Express todo service. Customers say **new todos come back empty**, **bad input crashes the server**, and **the "completed" filter never shows anything**.

## How the API should work
| Method | Path | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/todos?done=true\|false` | List todos, optionally filtered by `done` |
| `POST` | `/todos` `{ title }` | **201** + created todo. Blank or missing title → **400**, nothing created. Title is trimmed. |
| `PATCH` | `/todos/:id/toggle` | Flip `done`. Unknown id → **404** |

## Your job
Make every test in `tests/todos.test.js` pass, then **Submit** to run the hidden tests too.
Don't change the tests or the API shape.
